{"id":"mahabharata-13-096","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":96,"title":"षण्णवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 96 · The oaths of the sages","summary":{"en":"Bhishma tells the old tale of the oaths taken on a pilgrimage, in which each sage and each king, such as Dhundhumara, Puru and Dilipa, names a curse he would bear if he were the thief. These oaths describe in turn the cruellest of wrongs, and the sages conclude by naming the reward of the one who keeps to the true dharma and the scriptures guarded by the sages.","kn":"ತೀರ್ಥಯಾತ್ರೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ಆಣೆಗಳ ಹಳೆಯ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಋಷಿ-ರಾಜರಾದ ಧುಂಧುಮಾರ, ಪುರು, ದಿಲೀಪ ಮುಂತಾದವರು ತಾವು ಕಳ್ಳರಾದರೆ ಯಾವ ಶಾಪ ಹೊರುತ್ತೇವೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಋಷಿಪರಿಪಾಲಿತ ಶಾಸ್ತ್ರ, ಧರ್ಮ ಅನುಸರಿಸುವವನು ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಲೋಕ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म तीर्थयात्रा में ली गई शपथों की पुरानी कथा कहते हैं जिसमें धुन्धुमार, पुरु और दिलीप जैसे ऋषि और राजा बताते हैं कि चोर होने पर वे कैसा शाप भोगेंगे। अन्त में ऋषियों द्वारा रक्षित शास्त्र और सच्चे धर्म पर चलने वाले को ब्रह्मलोक का फल बताया जाता है।","te":"తీర్థయాత్రలో చేసిన ప్రమాణాల పురాతన కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు; ధుంధుమారుడు, పురువు, దిలీపుడు వంటి ఋషులు, రాజులు తాము దొంగలైతే ఏ శాపం భరిస్తామో చెబుతారు. ఋషులు కాపాడిన శాస్త్రాన్ని, ధర్మాన్ని అనుసరించేవాడు బ్రహ్మలోకం పొందుతాడని అంటారు.","ta":"தீர்த்த யாத்திரையில் செய்த சூளுரைகளின் பழங்கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார்; துந்துமாரன், புரு, திலீபன் போன்ற முனிவரும் மன்னரும் தாம் திருடரெனில் எந்தச் சாபம் ஏற்போம் என்று கூறுகின்றனர். முனிவர் காத்த நூல்களையும் உண்மை தர்மத்தையும் பின்பற்றுவோன் பிரம்ம உலகம் அடைவான் என்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"തീർത്ഥയാത്രയിൽ എടുത്ത സത്യങ്ങളുടെ പഴയ കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ഓരോ മുനിയും രാജാവും, ഉദാഹരണത്തിന് ധുന്ധുമാരൻ, പൂരു, ദിലീപൻ എന്നിവർ, താനാണ് മോഷ്ടാവെങ്കിൽ വഹിക്കേണ്ടിവരുന്ന ശാപം പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. ഈ പ്രതിജ്ഞകൾ ഓരോന്നും ഏറ്റവും ക്രൂരമായ തെറ്റുകൾ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; യഥാർത്ഥ ധർമ്മത്തിലും മുനിമാർ കാത്ത വേദങ്ങളിലും ഉറച്ചുനിൽക്കുന്നവന്റെ പ്രതിഫലം പറഞ്ഞ് മുനിമാർ അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.96; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अत्रैवोदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nयद्वृत्तं तीर्थयात्रायां शपथं प्रति तच्छृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this subject they tell an ancient tale; hear what happened on a pilgrimage concerning oaths."}},{"n":2,"text":"पुष्करार्थं कृतं स्तैन्यं पुरा भरतसत्तम ।\nराजर्षिभिर्महाराज तथैव च द्विजर्षिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, best of Bharatas, a theft of a lotus was committed, great king, by royal sages and likewise by Brahmin sages."}},{"n":3,"text":"ऋषयः समेताः पश्चिमे वै प्रभासे\nसमागता मन्त्रममन्त्रयन्त ।\nचराम सर्वे पृथिवीं पुण्यतीर्थां\nतन्नः कार्यं हन्त गच्छाम सर्वे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages gathered at Prabhasa in the west and took counsel: \"Let us all roam the earth with its holy fords; come, let us all go on that task.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"शुक्रोऽङ्गिराश्चैव कविश्च विद्वां-\nस्तथागस्त्यो नारदपर्वतौ च ।\nभृगुर्वसिष्ठः कश्यपो गौतमश्च\nविश्वामित्रो जमदग्निश्च राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shukra, Angiras, the learned Kavi, Agastya, Narada and Parvata, Bhrigu, Vasishtha, Kashyapa, Gautama, Vishvamitra and Jamadagni, O king,"}},{"n":5,"text":"ऋषिस्तथा गालवोऽथाष्टकश्च\nभरद्वाजोऽरुन्धती वालखिल्याः ।\nशिबिर्दिलीपो नहुषोऽम्बरीषो\nराजा ययातिर्धुन्धुमारोऽथ पूरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the sage Galava, Ashtaka, Bharadvaja, Arundhati, the Valakhilyas, Shibi, Dilipa, Nahusha, Ambarisha, King Yayati, Dhundhumara and Puru:"}},{"n":6,"text":"जग्मुः पुरस्कृत्य महानुभावं\nशतक्रतुं वृत्रहणं नरेन्द्र ।\nतीर्थानि सर्वाणि परिक्रमन्तो\nमाघ्यां ययुः कौशिकीं पुण्यतीर्थाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"they set out with the mighty Indra, slayer of Vritra, the performer of a hundred sacrifices, at their head; visiting all the holy fords, in the month of Magha they reached the holy ford of the Kaushiki."}},{"n":7,"text":"सर्वेषु तीर्थेष्वथ धूतपापा\nजग्मुस्ततो ब्रह्मसरः सुपुण्यम् ।\nदेवस्य तीर्थे जलमग्निकल्पा\nविगाह्य ते भुक्तबिसप्रसूनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their sins washed away at all the fords, they then went to the very holy Brahmasara; entering the water at the god's ford, blazing like fire, they ate lotus stalks and flowers."}},{"n":8,"text":"केचिद्बिसान्यखनंस्तत्र राज-\nन्नन्ये मृणालान्यखनंस्तत्र विप्राः ।\nअथापश्यन्पुष्करं ते ह्रियन्तं\nह्रदादगस्त्येन समुद्धृतं वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some of them, O king, dug up lotus roots and other Brahmins dug up stalks there; then they saw a lotus being carried away, which Agastya had pulled up from the lake."}},{"n":9,"text":"तानाह सर्वानृषिमुख्यानगस्त्यः\nकेनादत्तं पुष्करं मे सुजातम् ।\nयुष्माञ्शङ्के दीयतां पुष्करं मे\nन वै भवन्तो हर्तुमर्हन्ति पद्मम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agastya said to all those chief sages: \"Who has taken my fine lotus? I suspect you; give me back my lotus, for you ought not to steal a lotus.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"शृणोमि कालो हिंसते धर्मवीर्यं\nसेयं प्राप्ता वर्धते धर्मपीडा ।\nपुराधर्मो वर्धते नेह याव-\nत्तावद्गच्छामि परलोकं चिराय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I hear that time is destroying the strength of dharma; that time has arrived and the oppression of dharma grows. Before adharma grows here, I am going to the other world for a long stay.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"पुरा वेदान्ब्राह्मणा ग्राममध्ये\nघुष्टस्वरा वृषलाञ्श्रावयन्ति ।\nपुरा राजा व्यवहारानधर्म्या-\nन्पश्यत्यहं परलोकं व्रजामि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Before Brahmins recite the Vedas in loud voices in the middle of a village to low-caste men, before the king looks at unrighteous lawsuits, I am going to the other world.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"पुरावरान्प्रत्यवरान्गरीयसो\nयावन्नरा नावमंस्यन्ति सर्वे ।\nतमोत्तरं यावदिदं न वर्तते\nतावद्व्रजामि परलोकं चिराय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Before all men despise their betters and elders, before this darkness descends, I am going to the other world for a long stay.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"पुरा प्रपश्यामि परेण मर्त्या-\nन्बलीयसा दुर्बलान्भुज्यमानान् ।\nतस्माद्यास्यामि परलोकं चिराय\nन ह्युत्सहे द्रष्टुमीदृङ्नृलोके ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Before I see mortals devoured by the stronger and the weak consumed, I will go to the other world for long; I cannot bear to see such a thing in the world of men.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"तमाहुरार्ता ऋषयो महर्षिं\nन ते वयं पुष्करं चोरयामः ।\nमिथ्याभिषङ्गो भवता न कार्यः\nशपाम तीक्ष्णाञ्शपथान्महर्षे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The afflicted sages said to that great sage: \"We did not steal your lotus. You should not make a false accusation; we will swear sharp oaths, great sage.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"ते निश्चितास्तत्र महर्षयस्तु\nसंमन्यन्तो धर्ममेवं नरेन्द्र ।\nततोऽशपञ्शपथान्पर्ययेण\nसहैव ते पार्थिव पुत्रपौत्रैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having resolved this, and thinking this to be dharma, those great sages, O king, then swore oaths in turn, together with their sons and grandsons."}},{"text":"भृगुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhrigu said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"प्रत्याक्रोशेदिहाक्रुष्टस्ताडितः प्रतिताडयेत् ।\nखादेच्च पृष्ठमांसानि यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus, when abused, abuse back; when struck, strike back; and let him eat the flesh of another's back.\""}},{"text":"वसिष्ठ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"अस्वाध्यायपरो लोके श्वानं च परिकर्षतु ।\nपुरे च भिक्षुर्भवतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be devoted to forbidden days of study, drag a dog about, and be a beggar in the city.\""}},{"text":"कश्यप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kashyapa said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"सर्वत्र सर्वं पणतु न्यासे लोभं करोतु च ।\nकूटसाक्षित्वमभ्येतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus trade everything everywhere, be greedy with deposits, and give false witness.\""}},{"text":"गौतम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gautama said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"जीवत्वहंकृतो बुद्ध्या विपणत्वधमेन सः ।\nकर्षको मत्सरी चास्तु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus live proud of his intellect, sell basely, and be a farmer and envious.\""}},{"text":"अङ्गिरा उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Angiras said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"अशुचिर्ब्रह्मकूटोऽस्तु श्वानं च परिकर्षतु ।\nब्रह्महानिकृतिश्चास्तु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be impure, a fraud in sacred matters, drag a dog about, and be a destroyer of sacred knowledge.\""}},{"text":"धुन्धुमार उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhundhumara said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"अकृतज्ञोऽस्तु मित्राणां शूद्रायां तु प्रजायतु ।\nएकः संपन्नमश्नातु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be ungrateful to friends, beget children on a Shudra woman, and eat his wealth alone.\""}},{"text":"पूरुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Puru said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"चिकित्सायां प्रचरतु भार्यया चैव पुष्यतु ।\nश्वशुरात्तस्य वृत्तिः स्याद्यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus practise medicine, be supported by his wife, and live on his father-in-law.\""}},{"text":"दिलीप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dilipa said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"उदपानप्लवे ग्रामे ब्राह्मणो वृषलीपतिः ।\nतस्य लोकान्स व्रजतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus go to the worlds of a Brahmin who is husband of a low-caste woman in a village with a well for a ford.\""}},{"text":"शुक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shukra said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"पृष्ठमांसं समश्नातु दिवा गच्छतु मैथुनम् ।\nप्रेष्यो भवतु राज्ञश्च यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus eat the flesh of another's back, lie with a woman by day, and become the king's servant.\""}},{"text":"जमदग्निरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Jamadagni said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"अनध्यायेष्वधीयीत मित्रं श्राद्धे च भोजयेत् ।\nश्राद्धे शूद्रस्य चाश्नीयाद्यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus study on forbidden days, feed a friend at a shraddha, and eat at a Shudra's shraddha.\""}},{"text":"शिबिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shibi said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"अनाहिताग्निर्म्रियतां यज्ञे विघ्नं करोतु च ।\nतपस्विभिर्विरुध्येत यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus die without having set up the sacred fires, obstruct a sacrifice, and quarrel with ascetics.\""}},{"text":"ययातिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yayati said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"अनृतौ जटी व्रतिन्यां वै भार्यायां संप्रजायतु ।\nनिराकरोतु वेदांश्च यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus beget children out of season, a matted-haired man on a wife keeping a vow, and reject the Vedas.\""}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"अतिथिं गृहस्थो नुदतु कामवृत्तोऽस्तु दीक्षितः ।\nविद्यां प्रयच्छतु भृतो यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus, as a householder, turn away a guest, be a consecrated one who acts at will, and teach knowledge for pay.\""}},{"text":"अम्बरीष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ambarisha said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"नृशंसस्त्यक्तधर्मोऽस्तु स्त्रीषु ज्ञातिषु गोषु च ।\nब्राह्मणं चापि जहतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be cruel and abandon dharma toward women, kin and cows, and even strike a Brahmin.\""}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"गूढोऽज्ञानी बहिः शास्त्रं पठतां विस्वरं पदम् ।\nगरीयसोऽवजानातु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be secretive and ignorant, recite scripture outside the proper place and with wrong intonation, and scorn his betters.\""}},{"text":"नाभाग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nabhaga said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"अनृतं भाषतु सदा सद्भिश्चैव विरुध्यतु ।\nशुल्केन कन्यां ददतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus always speak falsehood, quarrel with the good, and give away a daughter for a price.\""}},{"text":"कविरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kavi said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"पदा स गां ताडयतु सूर्यं च प्रति मेहतु ।\nशरणागतं च त्यजतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus strike a cow with his foot, urinate toward the sun, and abandon one who seeks refuge.\""}},{"text":"विश्वामित्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vishvamitra said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"करोतु भृतकोऽवर्षां राज्ञश्चास्तु पुरोहितः ।\nऋत्विगस्तु ह्ययाज्यस्य यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus work for hire in a time of no rain, be the king's priest, and priest to one unfit to sacrifice.\""}},{"text":"पर्वत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Parvata said:"}},{"n":34,"text":"ग्रामे चाधिकृतः सोऽस्तु खरयानेन गच्छतु ।\nशुनः कर्षतु वृत्त्यर्थे यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be made headman of a village, ride in a donkey cart, and drag dogs about for his livelihood.\""}},{"text":"भरद्वाज उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bharadvaja said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"सर्वपापसमादानं नृशंसे चानृते च यत् ।\nतत्तस्यास्तु सदा पापं यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the sin of taking up every sin, and of cruelty and falsehood, always be his who takes your lotus.\""}},{"text":"अष्टक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtaka said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"स राजास्त्वकृतप्रज्ञः कामवृत्तिश्च पापकृत् ।\nअधर्मेणानुशास्तूर्वीं यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be a king of untrained wisdom, self-willed and a doer of evil, ruling the earth unrighteously.\""}},{"text":"गालव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Galava said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"पापिष्ठेभ्यस्त्वनर्घार्हः स नरोऽस्तु स्वपापकृत् ।\nदत्त्वा दानं कीर्तयतु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus be the sort worth less than the worst sinners, doing his own evil, and boasting after he has given a gift.\""}},{"text":"अरुन्धत्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arundhati said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"श्वश्र्वापवादं वदतु भर्तुर्भवतु दुर्मनाः ।\nएका स्वादु समश्नातु या ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let her who takes your lotus speak ill of her mother-in-law, be ill-disposed to her husband, and eat sweet food alone.\""}},{"text":"वालखिल्या ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The Valakhilyas said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"एकपादेन वृत्त्यर्थं ग्रामद्वारे स तिष्ठतु ।\nधर्मज्ञस्त्यक्तधर्मोऽस्तु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus stand at a village gate on one foot for a living, knowing dharma yet abandoning it.\""}},{"text":"पशुसख उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Pashusakha said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"अग्निहोत्रमनादृत्य सुखं स्वपतु स द्विजः ।\nपरिव्राट्कामवृत्तोऽस्तु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let that Brahmin who takes your lotus sleep comfortably neglecting the agnihotra, and be a mendicant who acts at will.\""}},{"text":"सुरभ्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surabhi said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"बाल्वजेन निदानेन कांस्यं भवतु दोहनम् ।\nदुह्येत परवत्सेन या ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let her who takes your lotus be milked with a bulbaja-grass rope into a bronze pail, and be milked with another's calf.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":42,"text":"ततस्तु तैः शपथैः शप्यमानै-\nर्नानाविधैर्बहुभिः कौरवेन्द्र ।\nसहस्राक्षो देवराट्संप्रहृष्टः\nसमीक्ष्य तं कोपनं विप्रमुख्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Kaurava king, while those many kinds of oaths were being sworn, the thousand-eyed lord of the gods, Indra, delighted, looked at that wrathful chief of Brahmins."}},{"n":43,"text":"अथाब्रवीन्मघवा प्रत्ययं स्वं\nसमाभाष्य तमृषिं जातरोषम् ।\nब्रह्मर्षिदेवर्षिनृपर्षिमध्ये\nयत्तन्निबोधेह ममाद्य राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra, speaking to the angry sage, gave his own assurance amid the Brahmin sages, divine sages and royal sages; hear it, O king, as he said it today."}},{"text":"शक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakra said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"अध्वर्यवे दुहितरं ददातु\nच्छन्दोगे वा चरितब्रह्मचर्ये ।\nआथर्वणं वेदमधीत्य विप्रः\nस्नायीत यः पुष्करमाददाति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the Brahmin give his daughter to an Adhvaryu, or to a Chandoga who has kept celibacy, and bathe after studying the Atharva Veda, who takes the lotus.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"सर्वान्वेदानधीयीत पुण्यशीलोऽस्तु धार्मिकः ।\nब्रह्मणः सदनं यातु यस्ते हरति पुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let him who takes your lotus study all the Vedas, be of holy conduct and righteous, and go to the abode of Brahma.\""}},{"text":"अगस्त्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Agastya said:"}},{"n":46,"text":"आशीर्वादस्त्वया प्रोक्तः शपथो बलसूदन ।\nदीयतां पुष्करं मह्यमेष धर्मः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What you have said, slayer of Bala, is a blessing, not an oath. Give me my lotus; this is eternal dharma.\""}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":47,"text":"न मया भगवँल्लोभाद्धृतं पुष्करमद्य वै ।\nधर्मं तु श्रोतुकामेन हृतं न क्रोद्धुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Venerable one, I did not take the lotus today out of greed. I took it wishing to hear dharma; you should not be angry.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"धर्मः श्रुतिसमुत्कर्षो धर्मसेतुरनामयः ।\nआर्षो वै शाश्वतो नित्यमव्ययोऽयं मया श्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dharma is the height of the sacred word, a flawless bridge; I have heard that it is the seers' own, eternal, constant and imperishable.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"तदिदं गृह्यतां विद्वन्पुष्करं मुनिसत्तम ।\nअतिक्रमं मे भगवन्क्षन्तुमर्हस्यनिन्दित ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So take back this lotus, learned best of sages. Blameless lord, you should forgive my transgression.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"इत्युक्तः स महेन्द्रेण तपस्वी कोपनो भृशम् ।\nजग्राह पुष्करं धीमान्प्रसन्नश्चाभवन्मुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by great Indra, the ascetic, who had been very angry, took the lotus, and the wise sage became pleased."}},{"n":51,"text":"प्रययुस्ते ततो भूयस्तीर्थानि वनगोचराः ।\nपुण्यतीर्थेषु च तथा गात्राण्याप्लावयन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they went again to holy fords, roaming the forests, and bathed their bodies at the sacred fords."}},{"n":52,"text":"आख्यानं य इदं युक्तः पठेत्पर्वणि पर्वणि ।\nन मूर्खं जनयेत्पुत्रं न भवेच्च निराकृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever, attentive, recites this tale on every parva day will not beget a foolish son and will not be without form or standing."}},{"n":53,"text":"न तमापत्स्पृशेत्काचिन्न ज्वरो न रुजश्च ह ।\nविरजाः श्रेयसा युक्तः प्रेत्य स्वर्गमवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No calamity will touch him, neither fever nor sickness; free of dust and blessed, he will reach heaven after death."}},{"n":54,"text":"यश्च शास्त्रमनुध्यायेदृषिभिः परिपालितम् ।\nस गच्छेद्ब्रह्मणो लोकमव्ययं च नरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whoever meditates on the scripture preserved by the sages, best of men, will reach the imperishable world of Brahma."}}]}]}